IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Canada Disability Benefit Act and Regulations -- CALENDAR HELPERS.
--
-- Not a section of either text: the date arithmetic that the Regulations' month-by-month
-- rules need, written once. A "month" is held as any day in it.
--
-- The stable prelude has no YMD, so the shim below is defined here, once, and every
-- other module reaches it through this import (dialects.md: YMD rejects on main).

§ `Calendar helpers`

-- Year first, then month, then day. `Date` takes day first, so the shim reorders.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YMD y m d MEANS Date d m y

-- A number that increases by one for each calendar month, so that two months can be
-- compared and counted from without touching the days.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month number of` d MEANS
    DATE_YEAR d TIMES 12 PLUS DATE_MONTH d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the month of` d MEANS
    YMD (DATE_YEAR d) (DATE_MONTH d) 1

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the month of` d MEANS
    Date (`Days in month` d) (DATE_MONTH d) (DATE_YEAR d)

-- Month 13 rolls forward into January of the next year (the lenient `Date`).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the month after the month of` d MEANS
    Date 1 (DATE_MONTH d PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR d)

GIVEN day IS A DATE
      d   IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day` day `falls in the month of` d MEANS
    `the month number of` day EQUALS `the month number of` d

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later day of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier day of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- How many months you move forward from the month of a to the month of b.
GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of months from the month of` a `to the month of` b MEANS
    `the month number of` b MINUS `the month number of` a
